[file.1]
path = "buf.yaml"
lines = 31
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 31 lines. The eight v2 module directories and the sole sdk/third_party/proto ignore exist; BASIC, FILE_LOWER_SNAKE_CASE, UNARY_RPC and WIRE/WIRE_JSON agree with the root generation path in scripts/protoc.sh. No api/buf.yaml is read after decision 722. Registry rows 7.fmt-buf-yaml-j39, 7.fmt-api-buf-yaml and 8.cfg-authority-registry-modules have the documentation disagreements recorded separately; the source configuration itself holds no retired dependency. Existing TestBufLintWorkspace and TestBufBuildFromApiDirMatchesWorkspaceImage cover the intended configuration; they were read, not executed."

[file.2]
path = "rpc/bloom.go"
lines = 20
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 20 lines. BloomIndexes is a type alias and EncodeFilters/MatchFilters forward unchanged address, hash and 256-byte Ethereum bloom types to rpc/ethbloom. Read the helper and TestMatchBloom: the producer uses Keccak bloom indexes, empty criteria match, OR alternatives and AND groups agree. BitMasks is a compatibility export; no mutable request state, tenant selection or retired component is introduced by this wrapper."

[file.3]
path = "rpc/echo.go"
lines = 11
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 11 lines. Rows 7.go-newechoapi-j38 and 7.rpc-echo-echo agree: constructor returns *EchoAPI, exported Echo accepts and returns a JSON string unchanged, and both production API lists register echo. The integration hello request/response agrees; HTTP mixed-batch consumers also assert returned strings. node/rpc_restart_test.go uses the real constructor on both transports and proves listener closure/replacement. The handler is stateless and requires no durable recovery or privileged authentication."

[file.4]
path = "rpc/export_filter_test.go"
lines = 9
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 9 lines. Package-level test functions call the actual unexported setReceiptLogFeed and shutdown with *FilterAPI and *ReceiptLogFeed unchanged. pending_filter_test.go and synthetic_receipts_test.go use these functions and clean up the API. They are compiled only for tests and cannot become eth_ or pax_ receiver methods through geth reflection; filter state and shutdown remain owned by FilterAPI."

[file.5]
path = "rpc/export_info_test.go"
lines = 16
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 16 lines. Both wrappers are package functions, not InfoAPI methods, so the served-method set is unchanged. *big.Int, uint64, *hexutil.Big, context and errors are passed unchanged to the actual helpers. rpc/info_test.go consumes both signatures and asserts gas-ratio behavior, including accumulated receipt gas; the hidden-helper HTTP tests and served goldens protect 7002.3/7002.4."

[file.6]
path = "rpc/export_metrics_test.go"
lines = 11
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 11 lines. The test-only package function temporarily swaps the real metric.Float64Histogram and returns a closure restoring the exact previous instrument. served_labels_test.go registers that closure with t.Cleanup and sends real JSON-RPC calls after installation, avoiding the known global MeterProvider initialization trap. No receiver method or production route is added; no persisted metric state is implied."

