note = "Read all 21 lines. Row 7.err-evm-not-supported-32000-j38 agrees: Error returns Msg and ErrorCode returns -32000, including the compatibility alias ErrCodeBlobsNotSupported. Actual InfoAPI and DebugAPI producers and geth error serialization use this typed error; error_codes_test.go exercises the real dispatch/client decoder for unsupported methods. -32601 is a documented distinction for missing names, not a dependency on the CLI, hosted gateway or removed relay rows; registry false edges are recorded separately."

[file.14]
path = "rpc/test.go"
lines = 23
verdict = "issues"
note = "Read all 23 lines. Rows 7.rpc-test-incrementpointerversion and 6.go-evm-artifacts-cw20-setversionwithoffset-j34 agree on string/int16 arguments and the error-only result. Unknown pointer types return invalid pointer type; cw20 forwards the signed offset. NewEVMHTTPServer registers this HTTP-only API only with EnableTestAPI on a non-live chain, and GetVersionWthDefault separately ignores overrides on live chains. The shared unsynchronized test state and absent path/lifecycle proof are recorded; no mainnet exposure is claimed."

[file.15]
path = "rpc/unsupported_ethdb_test.go"
lines = 17
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 17 lines. Backend.ChainDb returns the real unsupportedEthereumChainDatabase adapter. Get and Has return errEthereumChainDatabaseUnavailable, and errors.Is checks the actual sentinel rather than fixture text. Read unsupported_ethdb.go: write, batch and iterator operations also retain explicit unavailable behavior rather than fabricating database contents. This file verifies its stated read boundary without claiming a durable Ethereum chain database exists."

[file.16]
path = "rpc/utils_internal_test.go"
lines = 26
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 26 lines. The test drives the real runWithRecovery and recoverAndLog path with a synchronous panic, observes the installed hook exactly once via sync.Once and restores a typed nil hook on return. Atomic hook storage and the typed-nil check agree with utils.go; the timeout prevents a missing notification from hanging the test. This is process-level recovery, not evidence of persisted chain state recovery."

[file.17]
path = "rpc/web3.go"
lines = 27
verdict = "clean"
note = "Read all 27 lines. Row 7.rpc-web3-clientversion and decision 710 agree on Geth/<os>-<arch>/<go version>; registry row 7.rpc-web3-sha3-j38 uses hexutil.Bytes in and out and returns crypto.Keccak256, not standardized SHA3-256. Both production transports register Web3API with the right connection label. TestWeb3Sha3HashesInput sends the known hello-world bytes over real HTTP and checks all 32 output bytes; served_labels_test.go also calls both web3 methods over WS. Transport request limits apply before hex decoding and the methods carry no tenant-specific or restart state. Weak version-value evidence is recorded on web3_test.go."

